# ==============================================================================
# CRISP 2.2 — Environment Configuration (.env.example)
# ==============================================================================
# ZERO MANDATORY VARIABLES FOR LOCAL DEVELOPMENT:
# The application starts and runs 100% locally with built-in defaults.
# All variables below are OPTIONAL and enhance specific capabilities when provided.
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. OPTIONAL: AI Security Assistant & Multi-Agent Swarm (Groq LLM)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# If omitted: AI Assistant cleanly informs the user that Groq is unconfigured.
# All risk calculation, correlation, NIST scoring, and dashboards remain 100% active.
# GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_your_groq_api_key_here
# GROQ_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. OPTIONAL: NIST National Vulnerability Database (NVD API 2.0)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# If omitted: CRISP uses the public unauthenticated NVD rate limits (5 req / 30s)
# and seamlessly falls back to the curated local CVE snapshot if degraded.
# NVD_API_KEY=your_nvd_api_key_here

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. OPTIONAL: Local Storage Paths & Runtime Settings
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Overrides default file locations if running in specialized environments.
# Default SQLite backend path: data/crisp.db
# CRISP_DB_PATH=data/crisp.db
# CRISP_CHROMA_DIR=data/chroma_db
# Custom Python binary path (useful for Windows virtualenvs):
# PYTHON_BIN=python